;; The module _io (PY6a), as the survey's §6.6 has it: _pyio is io's implementation. _io is made from the
;; stdlib's Lib/_pyio.py, run as the module _pyio with a stand-in io in sys.modules for its "from io import
;; __all__, SEEK_*, Reader, Writer" (io.py itself imports _io first); the stand-in is removed once _pyio has
;; run. _io's names are then _pyio's: open, FileIO, BytesIO, StringIO, the buffered classes, TextIOWrapper,
;; IncrementalNewlineDecoder, and _IOBase ... _TextIOBase, which io.py subclasses. open_code is open(path,
;; 'rb'). The builtin open is _io.open (builtins_open: the first call imports io). sys.stdin/stdout/stderr
;; stay the runtime's own text streams (sys.go).

